    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="f26ac265-476d-55d4-8aae-0f7f6562206d" activityNameId="4fe9469a-8627-501e-a6f1-508a1816801b" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Sewer system, construction, polymer concrete pipe, DN 800, profile 2A</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Sewer system, construction, polymer concrete pipe, DN 800, profile 2A
Modern Swiss und European technologies are applied to building machines, material production and building processes. 
UUID: f7cd2202-1384-4428-a91d-f0be7b53667b
This process models 1 meter of installed sewer infrastructure with polymer concrete pipe and a trench depth of 3 meters. This process includes the production phase (A1–A3) and the construction phase/ transport (A4–A5) for 1 meter of installed polymer concrete pipe, including trench excavation and backfilling. Disposal and deconstruction processes are excluded and modelled separately specific for each sewer system type. The operation of similar types of building machines across different processes is aggregated to one process.
Location: Switzerland
Technology: DN 800, profile 2A according to SIA 190.Trench depth 3 meters. Polymer concrete pipe, ID 800 mm, outer diameter 948 mm, wall thickness 74 mm, 476 kg/m, 2300 kg/m³. 
Time period: Review of data currency scheduled after 5 years.
Production volume: 
Sampling: 
Extrapolations: None
Uncertainty adjustments: None
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_f7cd2202-1384-4428-a91d-f0be7b53667b.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
